00\u0000�k\u0000\u0000docProps/core.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000Pc��\u0010\u0002\u0000\u0000\u001a\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000{n\u0000\u0000docProps/app.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000t?9z�\u0000\u0000\u0000(\u0001\u0000\u0000\u001e\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�q\u0000\u0000customXml/_rels/item1.xml.relsPK\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0012\u0000�\u0004\u0000\u0000�s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"LA VERNE YOUTH & FAMILY ACTION COMMITTEE\n  Minutes of the Regular Meeting\n  March 25, 2025\n\n1. A meeting of the Youth & Family Action Committee was called to order by Council\n  Member Rick Crosby at 5:00 p.m.\n\n  Executive Board Members present:\n\n  Executive Board\n  Rick Crosby, Council Member\n  Wendy Lau, Council Member\n  Brittany Allison, BUSD Board Member\n  Denise Fisher, Resident\n  Don Kendrick, Resident\n\n2. Review of Minutes  Minutes for the February 25, 2025, meeting were\n  approved with Council Member Crosby abstaining.\n\n3. SRO Report  School Resource Officer Eduardo Burgos updated the\n  committee on recent public outreach that he has been\n  doing at the schools. This included having Police Explorer\n  meetings as he is hoping to grow the program. Captain\n  Travis Tibbetts shared that the department participated in\n  Read Across America in early March.\n\n4. CRR Specialist Report  Community Risk Reduction Specialist Lonnie Shipman\n  was absent from the meeting as he was attending the first\n  CERT meeting of the season. CERT is the volunteer\n  Community Emergency Response Team.\n\n5. BUSD Report  BUSD Representative Steven Patterson shared that the\n  Open House season is kicking off at the school district.\n  He reported out on the YFAC and La Verne Police\n  Department presentation on social media safety that was\n  hosted at Roynon Elementary. Additionally, the district\n  shared about the effort increase and improve outreach to\n  the community when it comes to attendance concerns in\n  order to work directly with families and help them.\n\n6. BUSD Student Update  The BUSD Student Liaisons shared that spring sports are\n  going well. The Spring musical “The Guy Who Doesn’t\n  Like Musicals” is coming up and the pop concert will be\n  soon. They also shared that the Concert Singers &\n  Chamber Singers are going to New York and singing at\n  Carnegie Hall.\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes February 25, 2025, page 2\n\n7. Utility Box Art Project  Senior Management Analyst Erin Beilstein shared an\n  update with the group regarding the Utility Box Art Project,\n  noting that the application was now live and on the City’s\n  website. She mentioned that a social media post had\n  been shared on the City’s socials. There was further\n  conversation about outreach and the school district\n  committed to sending out information about the project\n  as well.\n\n8. Parent Education Night  The Parent Education night hosted between YFAC, the\n  La Verne Police Department, and the District is coming\n  was held on March 18th at Roynon Elementary School.\n  Sergeant Flores presented on Internet Safety and how to\n  keep children safe on the internet.  There were\n  approximately 15 participants in this first session. Council\n  Member Crosby shared that he would like to see if YFAC\n  and LVPD could host this at all the elementary schools,\n  and there was discussion on how we could do that and\n  make it available to as many people as possible. The\n  Police Department also shared that they would like to do\n  an informational campaign online with the information\n  shared by Sergeant Flores.\n\n9. Fall 2025 Project & Funding Discussion\n\n  Council Member Crosby proposed that putting the Parent\n  Education night on the agenda for the fall 2025 projects\n  would be a good idea. Community Member Kendrick also\n  shared that he would like to hear from the school\n  counselors and have them be active members of YFAC\n  to help share with the committee about issues facing\n  students today. Council Member Lau shared that\n  organizations like Tri-City Mental Health Services is an\n  opportunity for YFAC to boost programs and services\n  already available to our community. She suggested that\n  YFAC members identify organizations that are currently\n  serving the city for further discussion with the committee\n  on how we can support those organizations and their\n  programs.\n\n10. Public Comment  The La Verne Historical Society shared about a project\n  that they are taking on as part of the Egg-cellent\n  Adventure. They asked if YFAC committee members\n  would be able to judge the coloring contest they are\n  hosting. Resident Fisher discussed concerns about lock\n  downs and school shootings with LVPD and district\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes February 25, 2025, page 3\n\n  personnel. There was agreement that further discussion\n  with the groups should continue. The Community Ministry\n  expressed thanks to School Resource Officer Burgos for\n  taking time to talk with the students in their program,\n  providing them with a safe environment to ask questions.\n  They also thanked La Verne Fire Department personnel\n  for supporting their family members through the\n  Leukemia Foundation Stair Climb in Seattle. Council\n  Member Lau shared with the group that ULV Athletic\n  Department was hosting its annual community day soon.\n\n11. Next Meeting  The next YFAC meeting was scheduled for April 22, 2025\n  at 5:00pm.\n\n12. Adjournment  The meeting was adjourned at 6:07 p.m.\n\nRespectfully submitted,\n\nErin Beilstein\nSenior Management Analyst"}